diff --git a/crates/ui/src/state_view.rs b/crates/ui/src/state_view.rs
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..3d5518a4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/ui/src/state_view.rs
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+//! The view preferences on the State (issue #645, the toggle asked on
+//! top of #727): the gizmo-name flag is `camcraft_app::view` preference
+//! state - read once at startup from the per-user file, written back
+//! the moment the browser checkbox flips it. The flag itself is view
+//! state like the camera (never a command, never on the history); what
+//! persists is the user's choice, so the next run starts the way this
+//! one ended.
+//! Provenance: our own wiring over our own app::view; no HSMWorks material.
+
+use std::path::Path;
+
+use camcraft_app::view;
+
+use super::State;
+
+impl State {
+    /// Startup: the per-user view file (the real window only - the
+    /// headless suites never touch the user's file). A corrupt or
+    /// unreadable file starts at the defaults and says so on the
+    /// status line.
+    pub(crate) fn load_view(&mut self) {
+        let Some(path) = view::store_path() else {
+            eprintln!("view settings: no config folder - they last for this session only");
+            return;
+        };
+        self.load_view_from(&path);
+    }
+
+    /// Read the view preferences from `path` and keep writing back there.
+    pub fn load_view_from(&mut self, path: &Path) {
+        let (prefs, note) = view::load(path);
+        self.show_gizmo_names = prefs.show_gizmo_names;
+        self.view_store = Some(path.to_path_buf());
+        if let Some(why) = note {
+            self.status = why;
+        }
+    }
+
+    /// The browser's "Show origin names" checkbox: flip the flag, and
+    /// with it take the user's choice out to the file at once - a
+    /// failed write is logged (by `view::save`), never shown over the
+    /// click; the flag in memory stays right for this session either
+    /// way.
+    pub(crate) fn set_gizmo_names(&mut self, on: bool) {
+        self.show_gizmo_names = on;
+        let Some(path) = self.view_store.clone() else { return };
+        let prefs = view::ViewPrefs { show_gizmo_names: on };
+        let _ = view::save(&path, &prefs);
+    }
+}
diff --git a/docs/decisions/727-viewport-gizmo-labels.md b/docs/decisions/727-viewport-gizmo-labels.md
index af59d909..bded6eb9 100644
--- a/docs/decisions/727-viewport-gizmo-labels.md
+++ b/docs/decisions/727-viewport-gizmo-labels.md
@@ -32,3 +32,37 @@ mean gating on `state.hover` in the shell's draw loop and leaving the
 producer untouched. `setup_chip_tests` filters plane chips by `" · "`,
 which never collides with an entity name - re-scope that only if names
 start carrying separators.
+
+## #645 - the names get a persisted switch
+
+**What was decided:** the review on the gizmo-labels PR asked for the
+names to be switchable, so `interact::overlay_labels` emits the name
+rows only while `State.show_gizmo_names` is on - a browser-pane
+checkbox, "Show origin names", right under "Show world origin axes".
+The `X`/`Y`/`Z` letters and every gizmo line and stroke ignore the
+switch: it quiets names and nothing else. The flag is view state like
+the camera (never a command, never on the undo history), but unlike
+the camera it is kept: a per-user `view.json` in the same config
+folder as the recents file (#662's folder resolver), written the
+moment the checkbox flips and read once at startup. Default ON -
+shipping the switch must not change a viewport a user already has.
+
+**Why:** names are what make several triads tell apart, but on a busy
+model they are clutter some users will want gone; the review asked for
+the toggle in view settings, persisted, default on. Persistence rides
+the recents' machinery (same folder, atomic write, corrupt-file
+tolerance) rather than inventing a second way to keep a preference.
+
+**Considered and dropped:** putting the flag in the project file (it
+is how *this user* likes the viewport, not part of the document - the
+camera is not saved either); a ribbon View menu entry (the browser
+pane is where the other viewport furniture already lives). A separate
+`view.json` sibling vs. widening `recent.json`: one file per concern
+keeps each tolerant read simple; if the maintainer prefers one config
+file, folding the `view` section into `recent.json` is a mechanical
+move of the same serde structs.
+
+**Cost to change later:** low. A new view preference is one
+`#[serde(default = ...)]` field on `app::view::ViewPrefs`, one State
+field, one checkbox; the old files keep reading and unknown keys stay
+ignored.

From 91e36cb90aaf6555d49767c46d0edb842e3debc5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tbrasselle <tbrasselle@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 10:27:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] tests: pin the switch through the painted shell and the
 config-dir override

Re-review asks on #645: a both-states structural check for the Show origin names switch (the seeded G54 triad's name row paints in the viewport on, drops on the checkbox click; X/Y/Z letters and triad strokes ignore it), and a gate for the CAMCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR override the persistence claim names (fake getter, as recent_files does; save/load round-trip under the override folder).
---
